@/chart

| Rank | Country | Approximate population |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | India (passed China about 2023) | ~1.43 bn |
| 2 | China | ~1.41 bn |
| 3 | United States | ~335 mn |
| 4 | Indonesia | ~280 mn |
| 5 | Pakistan | ~245 mn |

[info title="Why so uneven"]
Sparse lands share harsh conditions — the Amazon's forest, the Sahara's
aridity, polar cold, and the thin air of high mountains. Crowded lands
offer water, fertile soil, level ground, and jobs.
[/info]

## 4. Migration

| Push factors drive people out | Pull factors draw people in |
| --- | --- |
| War and persecution | Peace and safety |
| Poverty and unemployment | Jobs and higher wages |
| Disasters and crop failure | Schools and hospitals |

**Emigration** is leaving one's country; **immigration** is entering
another. Money migrants send home — remittances — is a pillar of many
economies.

## 5. India by the 2011 Census

India counts itself every ten years — decennially — since 1881; the
2021 Census was deferred. Key figures from **Census 2011**:

| Indicator | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Population | 1.21 billion (17.5% of the world) |
| Literacy | ~74% (males ~82%, females ~66%) |
| Most and least literate states | Kerala ~94%; Bihar ~62% |
| Sex ratio | 943 females per 1,000 males (Kerala 1,084; Haryana 879) |
| Child sex ratio (0–6 years) | 919 |
| Density | 382 persons per km² (Bihar densest) |
| Urban share | ~31% |

## 6. Settlements

@diagram tree id="settlement-patterns" layout="tree" aria="Settlement types from compact to dispersed"
  Settlements -> "Compact / nucleated"
  Settlements -> Dispersed
  Settlements -> Linear
  "Compact / nucleated" -> "Fertile plains and water points"
  Dispersed -> "Hills, forests, large farms"
  Linear -> "Along roads, rivers, and levees"
@/diagram

| Aspect | Rural settlement | Urban settlement |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Main occupation | Farming, fishing, forestry | Industry, services, commerce |
| Density | Low | High |
| Social life | Small-scale, kinship-based | Heterogeneous, anonymous |
| Settlement form | Compact villages or scattered farms | Nucleated, ever-spreading cities |

[example]
Compact villages cluster where water and fertile soil coincide, as on
the Ganga plain; farmsteads scatter across the hills of Uttarakhand.
[/example]

